# Cell from playpick, run to completion: mode=battleground map=flags
# spec=druid:feral style=auto view=1280x800 save=carried. 33.play already
# confirmed style=auto falls back to good on this non-touch viewport
# (no-autocast-toggle) and 34.play ruled out a suspected respawn-stall false
# lead (the player's own body revives at full health ~10s after death, same
# as the party). This run chases the match to its own end (FLAG_LIMIT=180s,
# src/sim/battleground.ts) -- direction.md's #7 asks for a good-style result
# on either battleground map to see whether active play (which this
# effectively is, via the auto->good fallback) turns the passive-body loss
# around rather than merely trailing less badly. Chained play calls with a
# short wait between, per the driver lesson already on record: a battleground
# death trips play()'s own hero-null fault and cuts a long call short, so
# several shorter calls get further than one long one would.
open
tap battleground
tap map:flags
tap class:druid:feral
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot start
play auto 40
state
bill
wait 3
play auto 40
state
bill
wait 3
play auto 40
state
bill
wait 3
play auto 40
state
bill
wait 3
play auto 40
state
bill
shot end
says
